ivity to classify each error-severity item\",\"Native DRC/schematic-parity results (work/drc/drc.json) reviewed; error-type counts (padstack, annular_width, starved_thermal) and parity warnings assessed\",\"Dual-wideband CAN2 chain traced in native source inputs/project/wbo-can-trans.kicad_sch and work/netlist/connectivity.json: TJA1051T-3 pin identity (TXD1/GND2/VCC3/RXD4/VIO5/CANL6/CANH7/S8), CANH->/CAN2+ and CANL->/CAN2- polarity, TXD/RXD crossover to f042 wideband modules U1/U2, S-pin grounding, VCC=+5V and VIO=+3.3V supply assignment, NUP2105L ESD clamps and 47p filters, and 120R termination population state (R36/R37 DNP)\",\"Board placement of CAN2 parts cross-checked in work/geometry/geometry.json (U21, C29/C30/C33/C34, R36 pads and nets consistent with schematic)\",\"VR conditioner front end checked: MAX9924 input network (R25-R28 4.7k pairs, C23 1n, DNP R29/R32/R33), BIAS divider (R30/R31 1k with C24 1u), open-drain output pull-up R34 to +3.3V, JP1 mode strap bridged to +5V\",\"ETB TLE9201SG safe-state check: DIS pins pulled up via R35/R5 10k to +3.3V (drivers disabled by default); VS on fused 12V rail\",\"Power rail distribution sampled across +5V, +3.3V, 12V_MR/12V_MR_FUSE nets; wideband module SEL strap difference (U1 SEL_1=GND vs U2 SEL_2=+5V) noted as plausible address selection\",\"Netlist/geometry consistency: 139 components, 199 nets, 10 DNP refs, 0 unconnected items in both netlist and geometry probes\"],\"limitations\":[\"Several artifacts were truncated in the packet (drc.json, erc.json, geometry.json, design.xml supplied as prefixes), so error-severity DRC item locations and part of the ERC/netlist detail could not be inspected directly\",\"Custom-library parts (Simon:MAX9924, Simon:TLE9201SG, fome_modules:polygonus, f042_wideband_module) could not be verified against vendor datasheets from the packet; pin-identity checks rely on the symbol/netlist labels\",\"Zone fill evaluated as saved per check limitation; starved_thermal errors may be fill-state artifacts\",\"Polygonus module internals (CAN1 protection, 5V-tolerance of module pins, 3.3V/5V rail sourcing) are outside this donor packet and were not verifiable\",\"No electrical measurements, simulations, or operating-condition data were supplied; review is static/native-rule and connectivity based\",\"The as-received lowercase 'VR conditioner.kicad_sch' filename discrepancy is declared out of scope for this disposable alias candidate\"],\"findings\":[{\"id\":\"f1-erc-errors\",\"title\":\"ERC reports 5 native error-severity violations (undriven power inputs, unconnected ~FLT, paralleled power outputs)\",\"location\":\"project/Polygonus-Universal-Base.kicad_sch (root sheet)\",\"condition\":\"Native ERC found 5 errors: power_pin_not_driven on hidden GND pin of #PWR01 (36.83,78.74), on A1 pin 8 VMOT (48.26,219.71), and on J2 pin 90 12V_IGN (293.37,173.99); pin_not_connected on A1 pin 2 ~{FLT} (38.1,224.79); pin_to_pin between J2 pins 40 and 41, both 'Power output' type on 5V_SENSOR_1.\",\"mechanism\":\"The GND, 12V_MR_FUSE and 12V_KEY rails are sourced only through passive connector/fuse pins with no PWR_FLAG or power-output pin, so KiCad cannot confirm the rails are driven; the DRV8825 fault output is left floating with no no-connect marker; J2 defines two paralleled pins as power outputs which conflict when tied. Electrically the rails are externally sourced via J1 and the ~FLT output is open-drain, so these are predominantly formal violations, but they mask any future genuinely-undriven rail.\",\"severity\":\"minor\",\"assessment\":\"defect\",\"evidence\":[{\"path\":\"work/erc/erc.json\",\"locator\":\"sheets[path='/'].violations: types power_pin_not_driven (#PWR01, A1 pin 8 VMOT, J2 pin 90 12V_IGN), pin_not_connected (A1 pin 2 ~{FLT}), pin_to_pin (J2 pins 40/41)\"},{\"path\":\"work/erc/console.log\",\"locator\":\"line 1: 'Found 353 violations'\"},{\"path\":\"work/netlist/connectivity.json\",\"locator\":\"nets '/12V_KEY' [J1.45, J2.90], '/12V_MR_FUSE' (sourced only via F1.2 from passive J1 pins), 'unconnected-(A1-~{FLT}-Pad2)'\"}],\"reasoning\":\"Confirmed native rule violations in the candidate schematic. Connectivity shows the flagged rails are fed from harness connector pins through F1, so no actual floating supply exists under stated use; the ~FLT output is a status output whose omission loses stepper-fault visibility but does not break bias or startup. Classified defect (tool-confirmed) at minor severity; remediable with PWR_FLAGs, a no-connect marker, and pin-type cleanup on the J2 module symbol. The 348 warnings (229 endpoint_off_grid, lib mismatches, 1 same_local_global_label, 2 multiple_net_names) are hygiene items consistent with the imported hellen-one/Simon libraries.\"},{\"id\":\"f2-drc-errors\",\"title\":\"DRC reports 13 error-severity board violations: 5 padstack, 5 annular_width, 3 starved_thermal\",\"location\":\"project/Polygonus-Universal-Base.kicad_pcb\",\"condition\":\"The DRC check summary reports 142 violations with by_severity error=13, decomposed by type as padstack:5, annular_width:5, starved_thermal:3 (remaining types are warnings).\",\"mechanism\":\"Annular-width and padstack errors indicate drilled pads/vias whose copper ring or stack geometry falls below the configured minimum, risking breakout or unreliable plated connections at fabrication; starved thermal spokes risk poor solder joints or marginal zone connection on thermal-relief pads.\",\"severity\":\"major\",\"assessment\":\"defect\",\"evidence\":[{\"path\":\"work/drc/drc.json\",\"locator\":\"header/summary region: 'included_severities' and check details by_type {padstack:5, annular_width:5, starved_thermal:3}; error items fall beyond the 100000-byte included prefix\"},{\"path\":\"work/drc/console.log\",\"locator\":\"'Found 142 violations / 0 unconnected items / 114 schematic parity issues'\"}],\"reasoning\":\"Error-severity counts are native tool evidence, so this is reported as a defect even though the individual item coordinates lie past the truncated portion of drc.json and could not be inspected. The starved_thermal subset may be an artifact of the as-saved zone fill (the check explicitly forbade a refill pass), but annular-width/padstack errors are fill-independent and fabrication-relevant. Exact nets/locations need the full drc.json to disposition; severity major because annular/padstack errors can gate manufacturing.\"},{\"id\":\"f3-can2-termination-dnp\",\"title\":\"Both CAN2 120R termination resistors (R36, R37) are DNP; internal wideband bus unterminated as saved\",\"location\":\"project/wbo-can-trans.kicad_sch (both instances /WBO-CAN-TRANS/ and /WBO-CAN-TRANS1/), refs R36/R37\",\"condition\":\"The single sheet's 120R termination resistor is marked (dnp yes)/(in_bom no), so both hierarchy instances (R36 and R37) are DNP. The /CAN2+ and /CAN2- bus carries both wideband controllers (U1/U2 via U20/U21) and is also brought out on J1 pins 15/11 and J2 pins 73/74.\",\"mechanism\":\"With both terminations unpopulated, the internal CAN2 segment between the two TJA1051T-3 transceivers and the Polygonus module has no differential termination unless the builder populates R36/R37 or supplies external termination on the harness. An unterminated or singly-terminated high-speed CAN bus suffers reflections and bit errors, degrading or breaking wideband communication the README describes as internal to CAN bus #2.\",\"severity\":\"minor\",\"assessment\":\"concern\",\"evidence\":[{\"path\":\"inputs/project/wbo-can-trans.kicad_sch\",\"locator\":\"symbol Device:R uuid d69380f9-5487-4782-9ce9-0690df62e543, Value '120', '(in_bom no)…(dnp yes)', instances R36 (/2889b04e…) and R37 (/10870bd0…)\"},{\"path\":\"work/netlist/connectivity.json\",\"locator\":\"components R36/R37 dnp:true; nets '/CAN2+' [C29.2,C33.2,D10.1,D11.1,J1.15,J2.73,R36.1,R37.1,U20.7,U21.7] and '/CAN2-'\"},{\"path\":\"work/geometry/geometry.json\",\"locator\":\"footprint R36 dnp:true, pads on /CAN2+ and /CAN2- near (175.0,142.1)\"}],\"reasoning\":\"Placement of the two 120R resistors near the two transceivers (x~81.6 and x~175.0) is a correct two-end termination scheme when both are populated (60R differential). Defaulting both to DNP is plausibly intentional because the bus is exposed on J1 for external extension, so termination choice is deferred to the builder; but nothing in the packet documents that, and the stated scope highlights 'internal dual-wideband CAN termination'. Labeled a concern, not a defect, since the DNP state may be a deliberate build option rather than an error.\"},{\"id\":\"f4-vr-input-polarity\",\"title\":\"CRANK+ / CRANK- connector signals arrive inverted at the MAX9924 differential inputs\",\"location\":\"VR Conditioner sheet (/76f66c7e-94ea-4f9a-aa2e-a01725934e38/), U10 with R25-R28\",\"condition\":\"Per the netlist, '/CRANK +' (J1.59) feeds R25 then R27 into U10 pin 2 (IN-), while '/CRANK -' (J1.55) feeds R26 then R28 into U10 pin 1 (IN+). The connector-positive signal lands on the inverting input and vice versa.\",\"mechanism\":\"For a VR zero-cross conditioner, swapping the differential inputs inverts the output edge relative to the sensor's true-zero crossing direction, which shifts which tooth edge the ECU triggers on. If firmware or documentation assumes the conventional VR+ -> IN+ mapping, crank timing edge selection would be inverted.\",\"severity\":\"minor\",\"assessment\":\"concern\",\"evidence\":[{\"path\":\"work/netlist/connectivity.json\",\"locator\":\"nets '/CRANK +':[J1.59,R25.2]; 'Net-(R25-Pad1)':[R25.1,R27.2]; 'Net-(U10-IN-)':[C23.1,R27.1,R29.2,U10.2]; '/CRANK -':[J1.55,R26.2]; 'Net-(R26-Pad1)':[R26.1,R28.2]; 'Net-(U10-IN+)':[C23.2,R28.1,R29.1,U10.1]\"},{\"path\":\"work/geometry/geometry.json\",\"locator\":\"U10 pads 1/2 on Net-(U10-IN+)/Net-(U10-IN-); R27/R28 pad nets consistent\"}],\"reasoning\":\"The input network itself (series 4.7k pairs, 1n differential C23, DNP attenuator/hysteresis options R29/R32/R33, BIAS at mid-rail via R30/R31/C24, pull-up R34 on the output) matches a standard MAX9924 differential VR application; only the +/- assignment relative to the connector labels is reversed. This is frequently an intentional edge-polarity choice (or the harness labels are arbitrary), and firmware can select the trigger edge, so it is a concern to confirm against FOME conventions rather than an evidence-proven defect. The symbol is from the custom 'Simon' library and the MAX9924 pin names come from the netlist labels; no datasheet was available in the packet to independently confirm pin 1/2 identity.\"},{\"id\":\"f5-j2-footprint-substitution\",\"title\":\"J2 module footprint on the board differs from the schematic symbol's footprint\",\"location\":\"project/Polygonus-Universal-Base.kicad_pcb, footprint J2 at (136.57, 99.21)\",\"condition\":\"Schematic parity reports: 'Simon:Polygonus-With-USB-SWD doesn't match footprint given by symbol (fome_modules:polygonus)' for J2, plus a BOM-attribute mismatch on the same footprint.\",\"mechanism\":\"All 107 Polygonus module pins (power, CAN, all I/O) route through J2. If the substituted footprint's pad numbering or geometry differed from the symbol's intended footprint, every module connection would be at risk. The parity check only compares footprint names/fields, not pad-to-pin compatibility.\",\"severity\":\"minor\",\"assessment\":\"concern\",\"evidence\":[{\"path\":\"work/drc/drc.json\",\"locator\":\"schematic_parity items for 'Footprint J2' uuid f447e585-df78-4239-b8cb-4653b3837bb1: footprint_symbol_mismatch (name) and attributes mismatch\"},{\"path\":\"work/netlist/connectivity.json\",\"locator\":\"component J2 footprint 'fome_modules:polygonus'; J2 pin nets populated throughout (e.g. /CAN2+ J2.73, +5V J2.81, +3.3V J2.82)\"}],\"reasoning\":\"The board netlist shows J2 pads carrying the expected nets and DRC reports 0 unconnected items, which indicates the substituted footprint's pad numbers do map to the schematic pins, so this is most likely a deliberate variant footprint (adding USB/SWD features). Marked a concern rather than a defect: pad-number mapping is validated by connectivity, but mechanical/geometric compatibility with the actual Polygonus module could not be verified from the packet.\"},{\"id\":\"f6-can1-no-protection\",\"title\":\"CAN1 lines pass from module to harness with no on-board ESD protection, filtering or termination\",\"location\":\"Root sheet, nets /CAN+ and /CAN-\",\"condition\":\"Nets '/CAN+' [J1.47, J2.93] and '/CAN-' [J1.46, J2.94] contain only the harness connector and the module header: no NUP2105L clamp, no 47p filter caps, and no termination option, in contrast to the CAN2 bus which has all three.\",\"mechanism\":\"If the Polygonus brain module does not carry its own CAN1 ESD protection, the primary vehicle CAN bus would be exposed to automotive transients directly at the module transceiver; absence of any base-board termination option also forces termination entirely into the harness.\",\"severity\":\"info\",\"assessment\":\"concern\",\"evidence\":[{\"path\":\"work/netlist/connectivity.json\",\"locator\":\"nets '/CAN+':[J1.47,J2.93] and '/CAN-':[J1.46,J2.94] vs '/CAN2+'/'/CAN2-' containing D10/D11 (NUP2105L) and C29/C30/C33/C34\"},{\"path\":\"inputs/project/README.md\",\"locator\":\"Features/Connectivity: 'Dual CAN'\"}],\"reasoning\":\"This is consistent with the declared modular architecture: the CAN1 transceiver lives on the Polygonus module, which may include its own protection and termination, and the donor review explicitly excludes integrated module coverage and automotive transient qualification. Reported as an informational concern so the asymmetry versus CAN2 is dispositioned deliberately rather than by omission.\"}]}","structured_output":{"schema":"agent-ee.review/1","candidate_id":"2767e5a30de2c3bcdee814eda2dbc63cc460f744b8029c74079b8feea3e0ae9b","run_id":"127a9e8e-5b06-4239-87ce-8ad95a4c01af","packet_sha256":"45933e29c78fa681b6a813c861b829f25710437d532eee33a5be27ae534e3bec","role":"circui