bels is reversed. This is frequently an intentional edge-polarity choice (or the harness labels are arbitrary), and firmware can select the trigger edge, so it is a concern to confirm against FOME conventions rather than an evidence-proven defect. The symbol is from the custom 'Simon' library and the MAX9924 pin names come from the netlist labels; no datasheet was available in the packet to independently confirm pin 1/2 identity."},{"id":"f5-j2-footprint-substitution","title":"J2 module footprint on the board differs from the schematic symbol's footprint","location":"project/Polygonus-Universal-Base.kicad_pcb, footprint J2 at (136.57, 99.21)","condition":"Schematic parity reports: 'Simon:Polygonus-With-USB-SWD doesn't match footprint given by symbol (fome_modules:polygonus)' for J2, plus a BOM-attribute mismatch on the same footprint.","mechanism":"All 107 Polygonus module pins (power, CAN, all I/O) route through J2. If the substituted footprint's pad numbering or geometry differed from the symbol's intended footprint, every module connection would be at risk. The parity check only compares footprint names/fields, not pad-to-pin compatibility.","severity":"minor","assessment":"concern","evidence":[{"path":"work/drc/drc.json","locator":"schematic_parity items for 'Footprint J2' uuid f447e585-df78-4239-b8cb-4653b3837bb1: footprint_symbol_mismatch (name) and attributes mismatch"},{"path":"work/netlist/connectivity.json","locator":"component J2 footprint 'fome_modules:polygonus'; J2 pin nets populated throughout (e.g. /CAN2+ J2.73, +5V J2.81, +3.3V J2.82)"}],"reasoning":"The board netlist shows J2 pads carrying the expected nets and DRC reports 0 unconnected items, which indicates the substituted footprint's pad numbers do map to the schematic pins, so this is most likely a deliberate variant footprint (adding USB/SWD features). Marked a concern rather than a defect: pad-number mapping is validated by connectivity, but mechanical/geometric compatibility with the actual Polygonus module could not be verified from the packet."},{"id":"f6-can1-no-protection","title":"CAN1 lines pass from module to harness with no on-board ESD protection, filtering or termination","location":"Root sheet, nets /CAN+ and /CAN-","condition":"Nets '/CAN+' [J1.47, J2.93] and '/CAN-' [J1.46, J2.94] contain only the harness connector and the module header: no NUP2105L clamp, no 47p filter caps, and no termination option, in contrast to the CAN2 bus which has all three.","mechanism":"If the Polygonus brain module does not carry its own CAN1 ESD protection, the primary vehicle CAN bus would be exposed to automotive transients directly at the module transceiver; absence of any base-board termination option also forces termination entirely into the harness.","severity":"info","assessment":"concern","evidence":[{"path":"work/netlist/connectivity.json","locator":"nets '/CAN+':[J1.47,J2.93] and '/CAN-':[J1.46,J2.94] vs '/CAN2+'/'/CAN2-' containing D10/D11 (NUP2105L) and C29/C30/C33/C34"},{"path":"inputs/project/README.md","locator":"Features/Connectivity: 'Dual CAN'"}],"reasoning":"This is consistent with the declared modular architecture: the CAN1 transceiver lives on the Polygonus module, which may include its own protection and termination, and the donor review explicitly excludes integrated module coverage and automotive transient qualification. Reported as an informational concern so the asymmetry versus CAN2 is dispositioned deliberately rather than by omission."}]},"ttft_ms":153832,"type":"result","duration_ms":238089,"uuid":"777434c2-c63e-4651-a40e-ca11743b545e","ttft_stream_ms":4045,"time_to_request_ms":240,"first_content_frame_ms":4045,"queued_turn_count":0,"result_index":0}
